<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output up 0.5% yr/yr in October.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output up 0.5% yr/yr in October.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    Oct 96     Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   100.7	110.8	    100.2</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months</p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) Oct 96     Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p> industry as a whole		  94.6	 94.5	     94.2</p>
<p> construction industry		76.7	 76.4	     82.1</p>
<p> investment goods		    100.5	100.8	     98.1</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
